Fats and Oils: Oilseed Crushings, Production, Consumption 
and Stocks

ISSN: 2379-9862

Released October 1, 2026, by the National Agricultural Statistics Service 
(NASS), Agricultural Statistics Board, United States Department of 
Agriculture (USDA).

Highlights

July 2026 contained 31 days.
August 2026 contained 31 days.

Soybeans crushed for crude oil was 6.29 million tons (210 million bushels) in 
August 2026, compared with 
6.66 million tons (222 million bushels) in July 2026 and 5.94 million tons 
(198 million bushels) in August 2025. Crude oil produced was 2.45 billion 
pounds, down 5 percent from July 2026 but up 4 percent from August 2025. 
Soybean once refined oil production at 2.00 billion pounds during August 2026 
decreased 1 percent from July 2026 but increased 6 percent from August 2025.

Canola seeds crushed for crude oil was 229,809 tons in August 2026, compared 
with 225,468 tons in 
July 2026 and 197,469 tons in August 2025. Canola crude oil produced was 182 
million pounds, down 1 percent from July 2026 but up 14 percent from August 
2025. Canola once refined oil production, at 175 million pounds during August 
2026, was down 7 percent from July 2026 but up 30 percent from August 2025. 

Cottonseed once refined oil production, at 22.0 million pounds during August 
2026, was up 16 percent from July 2026 and up 13 percent from August 2025.

Edible tallow production was 80.4 million pounds during August 2026, up 
9 percent from July 2026 but down 14 percent from August 2025. Inedible 
tallow production was 285 million pounds during August 2026, 
up 7 percent from July 2026 but down 4 percent from August 2025. Technical 
tallow production was 101 million pounds during August 2026, up 18 percent 
from July 2026 but down 13 percent from August 2025. Choice white grease 
production, at 104 million pounds during August 2026, increased 10 percent 
from July 2026 but decreased slightly from August 2025.

